cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite this archived version."
title: "artifact-rot: an observatory of the survival of code and data links announced in scientific papers"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Al Sarraf"
    given-names: "Zayd"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zay168/artifact-rot"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0-preregistration"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
abstract: >-
  Large-scale, replayable measurement of whether links to code and data announced in
  open-access scientific papers still resolve (stratified OpenAlex sample, 5 years x 4
  disciplines). This version freezes the preregistered analysis and decision rule
  (docs/analysis.md, docs/extension.md; French originals in git history) before the
  extension's verdict, scheduled for 2026-10-15.
keywords:
  - link rot
  - reference rot
  - research data
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - preregistration
  - survival analysis
